{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789969511,"nonce":"Wupvz//PkU7S85twYJ9RJ2VFnUg=","title":"zypy's built-in snapshot can outlive the compiler it was lowered with in an incremental debug build","message":"On the Mac worktree, after editing only crates/compiler/src (ssa.rs,\npool_alloc.rs, collector.rs, hir_interp.rs) and rebuilding zypy in debug\nwith cargo test -p zyntax_python, every program failed at once with\n\n    zypy: compile: Execution error: Lowering error: Lowering(\"Non-extern\n    function 'InternedString(SymbolU32 { value: 14 })' must have a body\")\n\nThe snapshot in OUT_DIR (python.zsnap) carried HIR lowered by a compiler\nwith an earlier BUILD_ID; usable_here() refused it, the library came in\nwith its bodies stripped, and lowering the bodiless declarations raised\nthe error above. Touching crates/zyntax_python/src/policy.rs made the\nbuild script rerun and the failure went away; the same tree built from\nscratch on the NUC did not show it.\n\nThe build script emits rerun-if-changed for policy.rs and\n../zyntax_builtins/src only, so it relies on cargo rerunning it whenever\nthe build script binary is relinked against a changed zyntax_compiler.\nThat held on the NUC and not on the Mac (rustc-wrapper kache is in use\nthere). Two independent fixes: make install fall back to lowering the\nlibrary with bodies when the HIR is refused instead of failing on a\nbodiless declaration, and have the build script emit\nrerun-if-changed=../compiler/src so the snapshot is always regenerated\nwith the compiler that will read it.","files":null}]}